WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.567 --> 00:00:03.634
-Welcome back. Hey, guys, if you
love seeing new inventions

00:00:03.634 --> 00:00:05.067
and you love brilliant kids,

00:00:05.067 --> 00:00:06.300
then you're really
going to love this.

00:00:06.300 --> 00:00:08.434
That's right, it's time
for "Fallonventions."

00:00:08.434 --> 00:00:10.534
Here we go.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:10.534 --> 00:00:12.367
-Welcome to Fallonventions,

00:00:12.367 --> 00:00:14.567
Jimmy Fallon's
night of invention.

00:00:16.934 --> 00:00:20.601
-Now, I love inventions
and I'm okay with kids.

00:00:20.601 --> 00:00:24.334
So we found some the best
and brightest kids out there,

00:00:24.334 --> 00:00:26.200
and I think you are going to be
amazed at what we came up with.

00:00:26.200 --> 00:00:27.734
So let's meet
our first inventor.

00:00:27.734 --> 00:00:29.234
Come on over here, Riley.

00:00:29.234 --> 00:00:29.734
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:29.734 --> 00:00:31.767
Riley.

00:00:31.767 --> 00:00:32.968
Hi, bud.
-Hi.

00:00:32.968 --> 00:00:35.067
-Nice to see you.
Riley, what is your full name?

00:00:35.067 --> 00:00:36.334
How old are you
and where are you from?

00:00:36.334 --> 00:00:38.501
-I am Riley Shove,
I'm 12 years old,

00:00:38.501 --> 00:00:39.934
and I'm from Manchester,
Connecticut.

00:00:39.934 --> 00:00:41.267
-That's right.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:41.267 --> 00:00:43.033
Thank you for being on the show.

00:00:43.033 --> 00:00:44.734
Riley, what is your invention?

00:00:44.734 --> 00:00:46.367
-My invention is the Play Box.

00:00:46.367 --> 00:00:50.067
I love spreading out and playing
with my toys all over my house

00:00:50.067 --> 00:00:52.467
but I really hate cleaning up
the mess.

00:00:52.467 --> 00:00:54.267
-Yeah, me too.
-So this is the solution.

00:00:54.267 --> 00:00:56.000
-So what do we have to do here?
Can I help you out?

00:00:56.000 --> 00:00:59.734
-So we can start by making
a little mess with these toys.

00:00:59.734 --> 00:01:02.467
-Okay.
Oh, yeah, I'm good at this.

00:01:02.467 --> 00:01:05.434
Okay, good.
Looks like my office floor.

00:01:05.434 --> 00:01:06.534
Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:06.534 --> 00:01:08.167
-Spread them out a little bit.
-Okay.

00:01:08.167 --> 00:01:11.501
-So then after you play a little
bit, you can then push

00:01:11.501 --> 00:01:15.067
all the toys back into
the middle of the Play Box.

00:01:15.067 --> 00:01:16.234
-Uh-huh.

00:01:17.634 --> 00:01:20.801
-Then fold up the four flaps.
-Oh, I like this idea.

00:01:20.801 --> 00:01:22.467
Oh, yeah, this is genius.

00:01:22.467 --> 00:01:23.868
Okay, wait a second.
-Yeah.

00:01:23.868 --> 00:01:26.100
-Yep, you're a genius.
-Thank you.

00:01:26.100 --> 00:01:27.334
-Yeah, okay.

00:01:27.334 --> 00:01:29.901
-Then you lift up
the side flaps.

00:01:29.901 --> 00:01:31.601
-Of course you do.
-Turning it into a box.

00:01:31.601 --> 00:01:33.067
-Yep, that's exactly right.
[ Audience oohs ]

00:01:33.067 --> 00:01:36.534
You are an absolute -- You are
a billionaire, my friend.

00:01:36.534 --> 00:01:38.167
I can't believe
I'm meeting you now.

00:01:38.167 --> 00:01:40.167
When you go to space,
you gotta let me know, okay?

00:01:40.167 --> 00:01:42.234
So I can come in your rocket.

00:01:42.234 --> 00:01:44.834
Oh, my gosh. Did I do it right?
-Yeah.

00:01:44.834 --> 00:01:46.133
-Look at that.

00:01:46.133 --> 00:01:47.501
And now you have just a box,
you can just travel with.

00:01:47.501 --> 00:01:49.667
-Now it's a box.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:49.667 --> 00:01:51.667
This keeps all the toys inside,

00:01:51.667 --> 00:01:56.400
and, as an added bonus, the side
clips can act as handles.

00:01:56.400 --> 00:01:58.501
-Little handles right there.
Not bad.

00:01:58.501 --> 00:02:00.300
This is brilliant.

00:02:00.300 --> 00:02:01.667
I do love this.

00:02:01.667 --> 00:02:03.000
Do you want to see an invention
I made?

00:02:03.000 --> 00:02:05.667
-Okay.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:05.667 --> 00:02:07.100
-You could be
a little more excited.

00:02:07.100 --> 00:02:08.767
But get ready for this,
this is really cool.

00:02:08.767 --> 00:02:12.267
This is unbelievable.
This is called a S'wig, okay?

00:02:12.267 --> 00:02:13.534
Oh, geez.

00:02:13.534 --> 00:02:15.501
Here's the way it works, okay?

00:02:15.501 --> 00:02:17.534
It's a stylish wig, alright?

00:02:17.534 --> 00:02:21.400
And concealed in the wig is
a drink bladder and a clear tube

00:02:21.400 --> 00:02:24.033
that drops down from the wig
so you can take discreet sips

00:02:24.033 --> 00:02:26.534
from the liquid hidden
in its pouch, in the wig.

00:02:26.534 --> 00:02:29.567
It's perfect for sneaking in
drinks into the movie theater.

00:02:29.567 --> 00:02:33.133
[ Laughter ]
Sporting events.

00:02:33.133 --> 00:02:35.467
Kids' recitals.
Whatever you got to go,

00:02:35.467 --> 00:02:37.100
you need to sneak a little --

00:02:37.100 --> 00:02:38.400
have a little sip
and here you go.

00:02:38.400 --> 00:02:40.868
It's just this easy.

00:02:40.868 --> 00:02:44.801
[ Laughter and applause ]
Ah, that was refreshing.

00:02:44.801 --> 00:02:46.434
-Okay.
-Thank you very much.

00:02:46.434 --> 00:02:48.334
I can see you're impressed.
Thank you very much.

00:02:48.334 --> 00:02:49.567
You can head over there.

00:02:49.567 --> 00:02:51.000
I know I just blew her mind
right now.

00:02:51.000 --> 00:02:52.267
She's like, "Yeah.

00:02:52.267 --> 00:02:54.701
That toy box was something,
but this is next level."

00:02:54.701 --> 00:02:56.334
Let's meet our next inventor.

00:02:56.334 --> 00:02:58.167
Sarah. Come on over, pal.

00:02:58.167 --> 00:03:00.100
[ Cheers and applause ]
Hi.

00:03:00.100 --> 00:03:02.300
-Hello.
-Jimmy. Hi, nice to meet you.

00:03:02.300 --> 00:03:04.300
-Nice to meet you too.
-Sarah, what is your full name?

00:03:04.300 --> 00:03:05.801
How old are you
and where are you from?

00:03:05.801 --> 00:03:07.167
-My name is Sarah Lamphere.

00:03:07.167 --> 00:03:10.200
I'm from Wolcott, Connecticut.
-Welcome.

00:03:10.200 --> 00:03:12.300
How old are you?
-I am 12 years old.

00:03:12.300 --> 00:03:15.234
-12 years old.
And now, what is this invention?

00:03:15.234 --> 00:03:17.567
What do you call this?
-I call this the Pet Puller.

00:03:17.567 --> 00:03:19.834
It's a safe way to get cats out
of carriers.

00:03:19.834 --> 00:03:21.834
-A safe way to get cats out of
carriers?

00:03:21.834 --> 00:03:23.100
Can you explain that more to me?

00:03:23.100 --> 00:03:25.501
-So, when I go to my mom's
veterinary clinic,

00:03:25.501 --> 00:03:26.801
I sometimes see the technicians

00:03:26.801 --> 00:03:28.667
struggling to get the cats
out of the carriers.

00:03:28.667 --> 00:03:29.734
-Oh, yeah.

00:03:29.734 --> 00:03:30.868
-Because the cats are scared,

00:03:30.868 --> 00:03:32.434
they're scratching,
they're biting.

00:03:32.434 --> 00:03:34.801
So I made a safe way
to get them out

00:03:34.801 --> 00:03:36.834
without hurting
the technician or the cat.

00:03:36.834 --> 00:03:38.968
-Okay, this is brilliant.

00:03:38.968 --> 00:03:40.501
Can we see it in action?

00:03:40.501 --> 00:03:41.868
Roots, can we get a gentle
drum roll please?

00:03:41.868 --> 00:03:43.968
-Of course.

00:03:43.968 --> 00:03:47.701
[ Soft drum roll ]

00:03:47.701 --> 00:03:48.968
Look at that.

00:03:48.968 --> 00:03:50.267
That is a brilliant idea,

00:03:50.267 --> 00:03:52.033
and it just moves the back wall
back in.

00:03:52.033 --> 00:03:54.334
[ Applause ]

00:03:54.334 --> 00:03:57.934
This is fantastic.
Is this -- Is this your cat?

00:03:57.934 --> 00:03:59.534
-No, this is not my cat.

00:03:59.534 --> 00:04:02.167
-Oh, wow. What a good cat.

00:04:02.167 --> 00:04:03.667
-I know.
-Do cats do this?

00:04:03.667 --> 00:04:05.601
I thought this cat would
just dive out or something.

00:04:05.601 --> 00:04:06.801
[ Laughter ]

00:04:06.801 --> 00:04:10.234
It's very simple
and it's a brilliant invention.

00:04:10.234 --> 00:04:11.734
I love this idea.
Congratulations.

00:04:11.734 --> 00:04:14.100
I have an invention
that's also very simple

00:04:14.100 --> 00:04:15.300
and brilliant as well.

00:04:15.300 --> 00:04:16.868
I just want to show you.
Check this out.

00:04:16.868 --> 00:04:19.567
It's called Over-Ear Earphones.

00:04:19.567 --> 00:04:22.300
Now look.
-They look wonderful.

00:04:22.300 --> 00:04:24.801
-Yeah, well, you don't even know
what they do yet.

00:04:24.801 --> 00:04:26.634
Watch what they do.
This is -- Watch.

00:04:26.634 --> 00:04:28.567
So basically, you put these on

00:04:28.567 --> 00:04:31.033
and no one even knows that
you're wearing headphones.

00:04:31.033 --> 00:04:33.467
-I wouldn't notice.
-Right?

00:04:33.467 --> 00:04:35.634
[ Laughter ]

00:04:35.634 --> 00:04:38.467
So you could be like at the
meeting or something like that

00:04:38.467 --> 00:04:39.868
and everyone thinks
you're listening.

00:04:39.868 --> 00:04:42.133
But really I'm actually just
jamming out to my favorite jams.

00:04:42.133 --> 00:04:43.367
[ Laughter ]

00:04:43.367 --> 00:04:45.267
Sarah, you still interested?

00:04:45.267 --> 00:04:47.634
[ Laughter ]

00:04:47.634 --> 00:04:50.133
Alright.
-I think they look great.

00:04:50.133 --> 00:04:52.267
-I couldn't hear what you said
but thank you, Sarah!

00:04:52.267 --> 00:04:53.767
Thanks for coming on the show!

00:04:53.767 --> 00:04:54.934
Why don't you head over there?

00:04:54.934 --> 00:04:59.334
We'll get our next inventor
to come on over!

00:04:59.334 --> 00:05:01.868
Come on over, Lucas. Lucas.
Where is Lucas?

00:05:01.868 --> 00:05:03.567
Hey, bud. Nice to see you.

00:05:03.567 --> 00:05:05.000
How are you? Lu-- Whoa.

00:05:05.000 --> 00:05:06.934
That was interesting.
What are --

00:05:06.934 --> 00:05:09.534
First of all, what is your --
Where are you from?

00:05:09.534 --> 00:05:12.167
What's your full name? Sorry,
it's reversible, this thing.

00:05:12.167 --> 00:05:13.968
It's great.
[ Laughter ]

00:05:13.968 --> 00:05:15.667
How old are you?
Where are you from?

00:05:15.667 --> 00:05:17.567
-My name is Lucas Kellogg,
I'm 14,

00:05:17.567 --> 00:05:18.868
and I'm from Shelton,
Connecticut.

00:05:18.868 --> 00:05:22.367
-That's good, man. A lot of
Connecticut love tonight.

00:05:22.367 --> 00:05:24.868
What is your invention there,
bud? What do we have?

00:05:24.868 --> 00:05:26.701
-My invention is
the Cold Clappers.

00:05:26.701 --> 00:05:28.767
And I actually brought you
your own.

00:05:28.767 --> 00:05:30.067
-What?
-There you go.

00:05:30.067 --> 00:05:31.367
-You're a good man.
Look at these.

00:05:31.367 --> 00:05:32.834
Cold Clappers?

00:05:32.834 --> 00:05:36.067
Look, and that's my picture
on there right there.

00:05:36.067 --> 00:05:37.968
[ Audience aws ]

00:05:37.968 --> 00:05:40.501
That's very cool.
But what are Cold Clappers?

00:05:40.501 --> 00:05:43.968
We're all enjoying this,
but what do Cold Clappers do?

00:05:43.968 --> 00:05:46.901
-Both my brothers play hockey
and I always go to their games

00:05:46.901 --> 00:05:49.100
and in the stands, everyone
is always wearing gloves

00:05:49.100 --> 00:05:50.534
because the rinks get cold.

00:05:50.534 --> 00:05:52.200
And so they try to cheer,

00:05:52.200 --> 00:05:53.667
but they can't
when they're wearing gloves.

00:05:53.667 --> 00:05:54.901
And so these go over your gloves

00:05:54.901 --> 00:05:56.667
and it allows you
to cheer for your team.

00:05:56.667 --> 00:05:57.968
[ Audience oohs ]

00:05:57.968 --> 00:06:01.467
-I think this is kind of
a genius idea.

00:06:01.467 --> 00:06:03.767
Can you show me how they work?

00:06:03.767 --> 00:06:05.868
-So, you just put it
over your glove like that

00:06:05.868 --> 00:06:07.467
and then you just start
clapping.

00:06:07.467 --> 00:06:09.501
[ Laughter ]
Simple.

00:06:09.501 --> 00:06:11.567
-Wow. Alright.
So what does it sound like?

00:06:11.567 --> 00:06:12.868
Let's go.
[ Clapping ]

00:06:12.868 --> 00:06:14.434
Oh, these are Cold Clappers.

00:06:14.434 --> 00:06:16.634
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:16.634 --> 00:06:18.300
Hey, I like this.

00:06:18.300 --> 00:06:20.200
You can put any team logo
you want on there,

00:06:20.200 --> 00:06:23.200
whatever, and then everyone is
clapping and clap for your team.

00:06:23.200 --> 00:06:25.200
I love this. Hey, you know
what could be fun though?

00:06:25.200 --> 00:06:26.834
This is kind of cool.
[ Laughter ]

00:06:26.834 --> 00:06:29.567
Here's an extra S'wig.
[ Laughter ]

00:06:29.567 --> 00:06:31.200
You put on the S'wig.

00:06:31.200 --> 00:06:32.868
Check this out.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:32.868 --> 00:06:34.601
You want to try these on too?
-Yeah.

00:06:34.601 --> 00:06:35.934
-Yeah, yeah. Check these out.

00:06:35.934 --> 00:06:37.767
This is going to be cool.
Look at this.

00:06:37.767 --> 00:06:40.467
And now you got
your Cold Clappers, and then --

00:06:40.467 --> 00:06:42.901
This is going to be bril.

00:06:42.901 --> 00:06:44.367
I think we're
on to something here.

00:06:44.367 --> 00:06:45.367
Ready, let's give
a little cold clap

00:06:45.367 --> 00:06:46.868
to our inventors right now.

00:06:46.868 --> 00:06:48.067
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:48.067 --> 00:06:49.601
Come on, everybody.
Come on back over here.

00:06:49.601 --> 00:06:51.534
You can go in the front here
if you want, Lucas.

00:06:51.534 --> 00:06:56.200
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:56.200 --> 00:06:58.300
I do have one more thing
I want to show you.

00:06:58.300 --> 00:07:00.267
We here at "The Tonight Show"
love supporting

00:07:00.267 --> 00:07:02.133
smart, talented kids
like yourselves

00:07:02.133 --> 00:07:03.901
and we want you to keep
exploring and creating

00:07:03.901 --> 00:07:04.968
and changing the world.

00:07:04.968 --> 00:07:07.400
So we're giving each of you
$5,000

00:07:07.400 --> 00:07:09.000
to help further your education.

00:07:09.000 --> 00:07:10.200
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:07:10.200 --> 00:07:13.701
Thank you. Thank you, bud.

00:07:13.701 --> 00:07:16.901
Lucas, you get a giant check.

00:07:16.901 --> 00:07:19.434
Sarah, you get a giant check.

00:07:19.434 --> 00:07:21.634
It's 5,000 bucks.

00:07:21.634 --> 00:07:23.033
Not bad, Riley.

00:07:23.033 --> 00:07:26.000
5,000 bucks right there
for you guys.

00:07:26.000 --> 00:07:28.801
My thanks to
Riley, Sarah, Lucas.

00:07:28.801 --> 00:07:29.801
Stick around.
We'll be right back!

